# Everything is LF in the repository and LF on checkout: the scripts here run
# on Windows, WSL and the Linux box alike, and a CRLF shell script fails with a
# syntax error naming a token that ends in a carriage return.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures say so rather than let git sniff them: a layout archive
# with its line endings normalised is a different crystal field.
*.npz binary
*.png binary

# The frozen vectors are hashed (tests/vectors/SHA256SUMS): their bytes are
# the claim, so git stores them exactly and never converts line endings.
# On 2026-09-25 the measured vector had been written by Python on Windows
# with CRLF; normalised on commit, a fresh clone would have failed its own
# hash. It was re-frozen as LF before the first commit, and this line keeps
# a CRLF editor from reintroducing the problem silently: the vectors gate
# fails locally instead.
tests/vectors/** -text
